      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T21:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`dumpAppProfile` will later on collect profiles for [all users](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java;l\u003d818;drc\u003d8cec104ae64bd45e1377d799ac4653fbce7fb631), so this means only a subset of them get flushed, doesn\u0027t it? Is this due to security concerns?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1229,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1229,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50204707_86843a3c",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1229,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-13T17:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is expected, and it\u0027s due to a security concern.\n\nThe concern is that, if this method waits for the profile flush for other users, the current user may protentially know the app running for other users by analyzing the time that the method takes, while they are not supposed to.\n\nThis feature is best effort to supporting a typical development workflow: install the app, run a few CUJs, and dump the profiles. In this use case, processes for other users aren\u0027t interesting, so it\u0027s not worth it to risk security for those.\n\nIn any case, we can never ensure profile flush for all processes, as there can be processes frozen or killed due to low memory. Supporting the typical development workflow is the motivation as well as a reasonable goal of this feature.",
      "parentUuid": "b44889ff_ec12f9bc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1229,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1229,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39ada7b6_fde429e2",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1229,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T21:52:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then wouldn\u0027t it\u0027d be cleaner if the profile collection also was restricted to the calling user, to avoid noise from other users?\n\nIf someone has a setup where the user calling this isn\u0027t the same as the one exercising the app (perhaps by mistake), then they may believe this flushing works when in fact it doesn\u0027t, and they won\u0027t get any clear indication that anything\u0027s wrong - there\u0027ll just be less accurate data.\n\nAlso, doesn\u0027t the collection of profiles from other users leak info too? E.g. if the current user deliberately doesn\u0027t exercise the app at all then the dumped profile will only contain usage data from other users, won\u0027t it?\n\nAt the very least, the docs for this method should be clear that it\u0027s restricted to the calling user, not \"all running processes\".",
      "parentUuid": "50204707_86843a3c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1229,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1229,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f73cfed0_fd301aaf",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1247,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T21:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While this is neat, it doesn\u0027t fully solve the problem with pid reuse since there\u0027s still a race from here down to `kill` below (`pidfd_open` doesn\u0027t cause the kernel to keep zombies, from what I can find).\n\nTo really fix it properly I think the only option is to use `pidfd_send_signal`. But to do that from system server would require passing over the pidfd from artd, and a new JNI wrapper to call `pidfd_send_signal`, so it\u0027s kind of tedious. Maybe that\u0027s reason enough to actually allow artd to send the signals? Then it\u0027d be a simple matter of changing `wait` to `sendSignalAndWait`. Otoh, from what I can see it\u0027s unfortunately not possible to have an sepolicy that restricts artd to only send SIGUSR1.\n\nThen again, I\u0027m not sure how serious a problem it is to send SIGUSR1 to the wrong process, so perhaps this race is fine?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1242,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1247,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca1c75be_1b4ccc41",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1247,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-13T17:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for bringing this up.\n\n[Here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/sepolicy/private/system_server.te?q\u003dsignal%20f:system%2Fsepolicy%2Fprivate%2Fsystem_server.te\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain)\u0027s the list of processes that the system server can send signal to. The consequence of sending SIGUSR1 to the wrong process depends on the process type. If the process is an app process, the signal just makes the process flush profiles and do a GC, which is probably fine; if the process is something else, such as a native service like artd, the signal kills the process.\n\nHowever, there are two considerations that are worth pointing out:\n1. The probability of the race is very low. Since we send the signal right after this check, the race can only happen if process being killed and the pid being reused all happen within such a short time window.\n2. The feature is for development only. The only entry point of this method is the shell command `adb shell pm dump-profiles`. No Java API calls this method. In the worst case scenario, an app developer sees the device crashing when invoking the command.\n\nThe alternative are, as you said, either use `pidfd_send_signal` in system server (which requires a JNI wrapper) or use `pidfd_send_signal` in artd (which requires an SELinux permission change). I think both are a bit tedious. Given the worst case scenario and its low probability, I think it\u0027s fine to accept the race.",
      "parentUuid": "f73cfed0_fd301aaf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1242,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1247,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de27a1db_caceda99",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/ArtManagerLocal.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1262,
