      },
      "lineNbr": 516,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T21:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not clear to me what this list contains. Is it all secondary dex\u0027es as well? If so that\u0027d mean we could be sending signals a bit wider than expected (in particular if the package is something like `com.google.android.gms`).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 516,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 516,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "758f49a7_28b4374d",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/Utils.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 516,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-13T17:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Secondary dex is an ART concept. The framework, including the package manager, doesn\u0027t know about secondary dex\u0027es. However, `pkgList` contains all packages that the process uses, so you are right in a sense that it includes packages that don\u0027t belong to the process.\n\nThat\u0027s why there is another filter above, to filter by uid (a combination of user id and app id). The two filters combined gives us an accurate list of pids for the package. This logic aligns with [the one that the activity manager uses to kill an app](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ProcessList.java;l\u003d3107-3118;drc\u003dac3be0cd06fea649aa4958c7cfe643fad811eb1a).",
      "parentUuid": "46bc9a1f_76d309b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 516,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 516,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e2647c0f_9f14caa9",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/Utils.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 519,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T21:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Docs are a bit contradictory - `ActivityManager.getRunningAppProcesses` claims it returns \"all running processes\" but then there\u0027s `IMPORTANCE_GONE` too, so I guess not really, then. (Of course the list is always more or less stale, but `IMPORTANCE_GONE` doesn\u0027t solve that.)\n\nBut nevermind that, with your condition I see `IMPORTANCE_CACHED` gets filtered out as well (and some deprecated values I presume can\u0027t occur anymore). Why?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 518,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7f9a697_60a57f0f",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/Utils.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 519,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-13T17:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I never saw `IMPORTANCE_GONE` during my local experiment. The intention of this filter is to filter out `IMPORTANCE_CACHED`. This is because cached processes can be frozen by [Cached apps freezer](https://source.android.com/docs/core/perf/cached-apps-freezer) and don\u0027t respond to signals.\n\nWith this filter, we may be sending the signal to less processes than desired, but it\u0027s still sufficient to support the typical development workflow: install the app, run a few CUJs, and dump the profiles. Again, we can never ensure profile flush for all processes anyway (thinking about LMK).",
      "parentUuid": "e2647c0f_9f14caa9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 518,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 519,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "8c4739ea30fc413b971274f013caee1e11e34b72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
